=base:main-content.cmark

# Changelog: tramaj-cli-rs

Release history of `tramaj-cli-rs`, the standalone Rust command-line interface over tramaj-rs. Releases happen when there are
major changes rather than on a schedule; each entry below is one version.
Every implementation has its own page like this one, and each page is
tagged so the site builds one Atom feed per implementation:
#changelog #rust #tramaj-cli-rs

The 0.2.0 entry has breaking changes to numbers:
[Migrating to integers and floats](/migrating-to-integers-and-floats.html)
says what to do about each.

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@version=import("changelog/version", {"package": "tramaj-cli-rs"})
.div(class: "changelog",
  $version({
      "version": "0.3.0",
      "date": "2026-10-24",
      "summary": "Follows tramaj-rs 0.3.0: \`?shape\` and \`~name\` markers, a symbol or term key of \`has\`/\`lookup\` is \`NotConcrete\`, and parse errors that point at an unclosed opener.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Templates can use \`?shape(key, shape)\` and \`~name\` markers. The form lowers at parse time, so \`evaluate\` and \`analyze\` treat it as the symbols it stands for."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking, symbolic mode only: a symbol or a term given as the key of \`has\` or \`lookup\` is \`NotConcrete\`, where it answered \`false\` or the fallback."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "A parse error for an unclosed \`(\`, \`[\`, \`{\`, string or interpolation is reported where the closer was looked for, with a line and column: \`at char 8 (line 1, column 9): expected ')' to close the '(' of .div at line 1, column 5\`."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered,
  $version({
      "version": "0.2.0",
      "date": "2026-10-09",
      "summary": "Follows tramaj-rs 0.2.0 to language v5: two number types, arithmetic, sorting and number formatting. On crates.io.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: numbers keep their type through the context and the output: \`3\` is an integer and \`3.0\` a float, and a whole-valued float is written with its fraction. An integer outside the signed 64-bit range is refused."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`evaluate --arithmetic\` turns the arithmetic profile on for the run. Without it, an error names the flag when the program references an arithmetic builtin."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`analyze arithmetic\` lists the arithmetic builtins a program and its libraries reference; \`analyze all\` carries the list under \`arithmetic\`."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`sort-by\`, \`sort-by-descending\` and \`format-number\` (decisions section 20) evaluate in every run, with no flag. \`round\` is the tenth arithmetic name: it needs \`--arithmetic\`, and \`analyze arithmetic\` reports it."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered,
  $version({
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "summary": "Rust port of tramaj-cli's Main.purs over the tramaj-rs crate.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Template + JSON context evaluation and the \`analyze\` subcommands, as a single static binary."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered)

